WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.650
- So in some sad YouTube news

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.520
that probably qualifies
for its own Darwin award,

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.800
a man was killed while
attempting to do a YouTube prank.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.420
Two individuals in Tennessee

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.810
attempted to prank-rob an individual.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.580
They were carrying butcher knives

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.710
and the would-be victim,
who was not in on the joke,

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.620
open fired and killed one of the two men.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.453
It's important to note

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.560
that we don't have all the facts here,

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.680
but it's entirely possible
that these circumstances

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.480
might give rise to self-defense.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.280
And self-defense probably makes sense

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.420
under these circumstances.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.640
In Tennessee, you don't
have a duty to retreat

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.500
if you are not engaged in illegal activity

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.960
in a place where you have a right to be

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.610
and you are reasonably worried

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.490
of an imminent threat of
deadly or serious harm,

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.540
and you think it's reasonable

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.060
to use deadly force to fight that.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.290
And here, two people
brandishing butcher knives,

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.250
threatening to rob you,
probably meets that definition.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.460
So let that be a lesson.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.280
Don't do stupid things
for internet fame or clout

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.023
and subscribe, or I'll see you in court.

